From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LNPANDY <lnp-andy@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:47:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Mac: fix Joy-Con press-to-join, official 0x057e deduplication
 and multi-pair haptics

Fix three Bluetooth Joy-Con regressions on macOS:
- Honor DM_PAD_PRESS_TO_JOIN=1 in joycon_attach() and claim a player slot
  in joycon_read() on the first face, shoulder, rail SL/SR, Capture or
  Home press, while claiming the secondary slot immediately when splitting
  a joined pair with SL+SR.
- Restrict joycon_is_gc_controller() to Apple's exact official product
  categories when a matching non-synthetic Nintendo 0x057e:0x2006 or
  0x2007 IOHIDDevice is present so third-party controllers with JoyCon or
  Joy-Con in their name stay active on GCController.
- Pair each Joy-Con pad group with its own GCController haptics instance
  via gc_tag capacity matching so rumble on slots 2..4 routes to the
  second physical Joy-Con pair instead of always targeting the first pair.

Add end-to-end regression tests in t_controllers_mac.m covering 0x30 input
reports with press-to-join, third-party controller deduplication, and
four-Joy-Con rumble routing.

Upstream-Status: pending [builds on 0074-mac-split-a-joy-con-pair-into-two-sideways-contr.patch and 0081-support-steam-controller-and-shared-mac-control.patch]
Reason: Honor DM_PAD_PRESS_TO_JOIN on Bluetooth Joy-Cons, keep third-party controllers named JoyCon on GCController, and route rumble across multiple Joy-Con pairs
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#740
